From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005
Subject: [PATCH] TEMPORARY: @companion dump - dump live shell identity and state

A diagnostic-only patch. Four attempts at "the companion ignores its skill selection"
were built on INFERENCES read out of log lines; this prints the ground truth instead.

Prints one @SHELL line per live population shell:

  index | name | class | owner_account | override_active | attack_n | buff_n |
  state.active | prev!=null | map_id2bl(id)==self | party_id | pop_is_companion

That single output settles, in one read:
  * whether the shell holding a companion index is really that companion (name match);
  * whether it received skill_override_active, which is what the selector filters on;
  * whether the engine can resolve it as a companion at all (pop_is_companion, which
    keys on party_id and so is false whenever a party rebuild zeroed it);
  * whether the shell is on the grid (prev / map_id2bl), which decides if it can cast.

Usage: @companion dump   (in game; output is @SHELL|... lines, @SHELLEND|n sentinel)

REMOVE THIS PATCH once the selector is confirmed working - it is not shipping code.
